                  Parameters for SPECSIM3D
                  ************************

START OF PARAMETERS:
0.0 0.0 0.0                   xmin ymin zmin  (coordinates of the first node)
1.0 1.0 1.0                   dx dy dz  (grid spacing)
64 64 16                      nx ny nz  (nodes per axis, nz = 1 gives a 2D field)
0.0 1                         nugget nstruct  (nugget variance, number of nested structures)
2 1.0 20 10 5 45.0 0.0 0.0    itype sill ahmax ahmin avert azimuth dip plunge  (itype: 1 spherical, 2 exponential, 3 gaussian)
4001 20 1                     iseed nreal ipad  (random seed, number of realizations, ipad: 1 = padded periodic grid)
example_cond1_gaussian_3d
2                             nout  (number of outputs; one code per line follows)
4                             output code: 4 = one VTK XML file <base>.vti with all the realizations (ParaView opens it directly)
3                             output code: 3 = raw float32 file <base>.bin (realizations consecutive, x fastest)
1                             icond  (0 = unconditional simulation, 1 = conditional: the conditioning block follows)
data_gaussian_3d.dat          datafile (GSLIB format: title, nvar, nvar names, data rows)
1 2 3 4 0                     columns: x y z value weight (0 = not used; z = 0 for 2D data)
-1.0e21 1.0e21                trimming limits on the value
0 0.0                         itrans (0 = data already N(0,1) or kept as they are, 1 = normal score + back transform), skmean (itrans=0)
-5.0 5.0                      zmin zmax (back transform limits, itrans = 1)
1 0.0                         lower tail: 1 = linear, 2 = power (omega)
1 0.0                         upper tail: 1 = linear, 2 = power (omega), 4 = hyperbolic (omega)
30.0 15.0 8.0                 search ellipsoid radii: maximum, medium (horizontal), vertical
45.0 0.0 0.0                  search ellipsoid angles: azimuth, dip, plunge (as in the variogram model)
24                            ndmax: maximum number of data used per node (<= 100)
